# HISTORICAL — DO NOT APPLY
#
# This defect was upstreamed. It is fixed in rustio-admin 0.33.1, at commit
# 5eb63a7e12ab279f9f5ccab09e01d7aeb99bc03f (tag v0.33.1) in
# https://github.com/abdulwahed-sweden/rustio-admin.
#
# hemsidor24-admin depends on that exact revision, so the fix arrives through
# the dependency. This file is retained only as provenance: it records what was
# wrong, what the change was, and that Hemsidor24 found it. It takes no part in
# a normal build and must not be applied to anything.
#
# The defect: orm::create and orm::update bound every Value::Null as
# None::<i64>, so PostgreSQL rejected any insert or update whose target column
# was not a bigint. An order with `notified_at IS NULL` could not have its
# status changed; the admin returned 500.
#
# ---- original patch below, unchanged ----

